Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-17-2001||12:39 PM||||Anyway to make the dash brighter?<P>It seems REALLY dim (maybe  we are just not used to driving it I guess?)<P>can stronger bulbs be used?<P>Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-17-2001||12:55 PM||||...you may even have some bulbs burned out- there's got to be at least a dozen in the cluster!  <P>You can get "hyperwhite" 194 bulbs from <A HREF="http://www.xtremewhite.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtremewhite.com</A>  they're not cheap, but they would help.  But I'd just double check to be sure that all your bulbs are currently good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-17-2001||01:15 PM||||Thanks for the info.. I will cehck the extreme ones out..<P>I did check my bulbs when I replaced my tach, so it might be a  bad ground yet somewhere..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-17-2001||01:44 PM||||I assume you have a reflective lit instrument panel, not one of the later model backlit ones.  My 85SE instrument panel is also very dim and I'd be interested in the Hyperwhites also.  Do they run hotter than standard 194s?  Would this cause a problem in the cluster?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-17-2001||01:53 PM||||Yep.. I have the stock orange 84 dash..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||10-17-2001||02:10 PM||||Nope... the hyperwhites shouldn't run any hotter than the stock 194's.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||10-18-2001||03:34 PM||||I looked at the hyperwhites on the web site.  The bulbs are around $8.00 each.  It would be cheaper to get a backlit instrument cluster from a donor than to replace all the bulbs with hyperwhites.||||reg||1
