Z||000010||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-18-2001||05:20 PM||||Thanks.. I will check them out also..<P>How much hassle would it be to change my dash color?<P>simple as changing bulbs or spraying the inside?<P>Think I might pull my spare dash out of my parts car and see what I can do  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||05:31 PM||||You definitely will need to repaint the inner dash piece... it's BRIGHT orange and will need at least a couple of coats of whatever color to cover it!<P>You can put different color bulbs in, but you'll still have the orange/black on the faces themselves.  If you want to, you can get some gauge face stickers to go over the current face (I've never done it to a front-lit before, but it should be pretty easy).  If you've got a spare dash assembly, go for it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-18-2001||05:41 PM||||I was thinking of using Aus's backlit faceplates he posted a few months ago and converting it to either green or blue (wifes request) If I dont like it, it should only take a few minutes to switch back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>much trouble getting the color switched also on the heater assy?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||05:59 PM||||I've been working on a climate control face- If it's the backlit one (like my GT has...) then it's the same process as the backlit gauge faces- Easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  I haven't looked into the non-backlit model yet (don't have one handy).<P>[EDIT]<BR>Oh yeah, this is the thread for my failed attempt at an indiglo-style backlit gauge without using an alternative light source. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011111.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011111.html</A> <BR>[/EDIT]<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-18-2001||06:45 PM||||When I get time to do them up, I will post a photo..<P>For printing out the faceplates, I was thinking of using photo paper with matte finish.. It would be thicker and may show up better..<P>think it would be worthwhile? ||||reg||1
Z||000015||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||08:40 PM||||I would even possibly skip the matte photo paper and go straight for an Avery Brand (or similiar) printable label.  They're about $15 for 25 pages at the local office supply store.  Then you can print them and stick 'em straight on- no messing with adhesive sprays or anything.||||reg||1
